{
  "id": "refund_reversal_no_network_ref",
  "title": "Refund processed as a reversal: succeeded without network_ref",
  "test_plan_vector": null,
  "spec": [
    "Platform Verification 4: MUST evaluate `seq` and `prev` continuity per `(iss, mandate_ref)` chain. A byte-identical redelivery of a receipt the platform already holds is ignored. A second, different receipt for a `seq` the platform already holds is `receipt_sequence_gap`; the platform keeps both.",
    "Platform Verification 5: MUST recompute `authorized`, `captured` and `refunded` for each chain from the `succeeded` events it holds, per Running Totals, and MUST check that `totals.mandated` equals the `payment_amount` of the Payment Mandate that `mandate_ref` covers. A receipt whose stated `totals` differ from these values is `receipt_totals_mismatch`. Recomputation stops at the first `receipt_sequence_gap` or excluded receipt in a chain: the platform does not report `receipt_totals_mismatch` for later receipts in that chain, because the events it holds are incomplete.",
    "Edge Cases, Pending movements: a movement may first be receipted as `pending`. A later receipt in the same chain for the same movement carries `status: succeeded`. Totals change only on the `succeeded` receipt.",
    "Edge Cases, Late network references: when a network reference (for example the Acquirer Reference Number of a refund) is assigned after the movement is receipted as `succeeded`, it appears on a follow-up receipt with the same `type` and `event.ref.processing_entry_id`, which does not change the totals. `network_ref` is optional on every status: a refund that the processor settles as a reversal of the original transaction may never have one. It is still receipted as a `refund`."
  ],
  "signing": "TEST-ONLY P-256 keys derived from fixed labels in common/payments/ap2_receipt_fixtures.py; deterministic ECDSA (RFC 6979). Never use them outside these vectors.",
  "notes": "The refund settles as a reversal of the authorization shortly after capture, so no network reference is ever assigned: the succeeded receipt for the same event.ref has no network_ref, and is valid.",
